# Template for scripts/screenshot/run.sh: renders the full 11-step wizard
# walkthrough against the fakepve fixture and screenshots the header of
# every step. @W@/@H@/@NAME@ are substituted per size preset by run.sh.
# Each "STEP N" block is self-contained: the wait/screenshot pair that opens
# it, then the keystrokes that complete that step and advance to the next
# one. Keystroke sequences mirror docs/assets/demo.tape (the human-paced
# README recording) with sleeps compressed for unattended batch rendering.
#
# The wait gates from step 2 on match the header's phase trail (connect/
# cluster/extras/review), not the step title: steps/register.go's deployPhases
# groups the 11 steps into those 4 phases, and the trail's inline dot ribbon
# tracks each step's position within its phase's visible steps — a string unique
# per step that (unlike the title) is never clipped by the header's width
# budget at 80 cols, verified by
# internal/tui/wizard/steps/register_test.go's
# TestPhaseTrailFits80ColsWithLongestTitle.
Output out/@NAME@.txt
Set Shell zsh
Set FontSize 14
Set Padding 0
Set LineHeight 1.0
Set LetterSpacing 1.0
Set Width @W@
Set Height @H@

Hide
Type `export PATH="$(dirname "$OKDCTL_DEMO_BIN"):$PATH" HOME="$OKDCTL_DEMO_HOME" OKDCTL_WIZARD_DEMO=1; cd "$OKDCTL_DEMO_CWD"; clear`
Enter
Show

Type "okdctl deploy"
Sleep 450ms
Enter

# ==================== STEP 1: the hero-hub ====================
# The hub's own gate, not the phase trail: "cluster status" is a verb only the
# five-verb menu carries, so the gate also proves run.sh's seeded okdctl.yaml
# loaded. Had it not, the hub would show its two-verb blank slate and the Down
# below would land on "quit" instead of "edit config".
Wait+Screen@10s /cluster status/
# The gate releases as soon as the matching text lands in the screen buffer,
# which on this screen is mid-paint: the hero alone is five (or ten) rows of
# block characters, and a Screenshot fired at the gate captures a half-drawn
# frame. Every later step gates on text the wizard paints last, so only this
# one needs to settle.
Sleep 500ms
Screenshot out/@NAME@-welcome.png
Sleep 300ms
# deploy is the first verb and deploys the saved configuration outright; the
# walkthrough wants the configure flow, which is the second verb.
Down
Sleep 450ms
Enter
Sleep 450ms

# ==================== STEP 2: okd version (distribution) ====================
Wait+Screen@10s /connect ✓●○ · cluster · extras · review/
Screenshot out/@NAME@-distribution.png
Sleep 300ms
Enter
Sleep 650ms
Down
Sleep 450ms
Down
Sleep 450ms
Up
Sleep 450ms
Up
Sleep 650ms
# Cursor freedom: up from the first patch (4.20.1) flows past the dropdown
# boundary back onto the parent minor row (4.20) instead of trapping there.
Screenshot out/@NAME@-distribution-expanded.png
Sleep 300ms
Enter
Sleep 450ms

# ==================== STEP 3: proxmox connection ====================
Wait+Screen@10s /connect ✓✓● · cluster · extras · review/
Screenshot out/@NAME@-proxmox.png
Sleep 300ms
Shift+Tab
Shift+Tab
Type "127.0.0.1:@PVEPORT@"
Wait+Screen@2s /127.0.0.1:@PVEPORT@/
Sleep 450ms
Tab
Type "root@pam"
Sleep 450ms
Tab
Type "demo-password"
Sleep 450ms
Tab
Sleep 450ms
Tab
Sleep 450ms
Right
Sleep 650ms
Enter
Sleep 450ms

